p.src:
The inner movement can be written as $\text{listening}
\xrightarrow{\ \text{attention}\ }
\text{insight}.$ The essential point is that insight is not set aside as a reward at the end. Anderson notices this: the insight must be present from the beginning as the two inquire together.

