p.src:
The first example is society’s immorality: $\text{negation of immorality}
\Longrightarrow
\text{morality}.$ This does not mean trying to be moral. Krishnamurti’s point is sharper: trying to be moral still belongs to conflict and becoming. Actual negation of immorality is already the coming into being of morality.

